      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What you're describing touches on a feeling of profound existential distance, where the concerns of others seem trivial compared to your own internal landscape. This sense of being on a different frequency suggests a deep disconnect from conventional human experience. It can be exhausting to carry such a unique perception, and acknowledging that disconnect is the first step toward figuring out how to navigate it. Consider journaling about the thoughts that make you feel this profound separation to help map out this internal world.",
      "source": "target",
